<%- include('partials/header') %>
<section class="page-hero compact">
    <p class="small-title">YOUR PRIVACY</p>
    <h1>Privacy &amp; Cookies</h1>
    <p>What Woodora remembers about your visit, and how to switch it off.</p>
</section>
<section class="section">
    <div class="card prose">
        <h2>Cookies the shop needs</h2>
        <p>The cookie named <code>woodora</code> keeps you logged in, remembers your shopping cart and protects forms from misuse.
           The shop cannot work without it, so it is always used.</p>

        <h2>Anonymous visit statistics (only if you agree)</h2>
        <p>If you press <strong>Accept</strong>, Woodora saves two random cookies and counts your visit so the owner can see how many people
           visit and which pages are popular:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><code>woodora_vid</code> &ndash; a random anonymous ID, kept for 1 year. It lets us tell new visitors from returning ones.</li>
            <li><code>woodora_sid</code> &ndash; a random ID for the current visit, which ends after 30 minutes without activity.</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>What is saved:</strong> the random IDs, the page you opened (for example <code>/products</code>) and the time.</p>
        <p><strong>What is never saved with a visit:</strong> your name, email address, password, IP address, browser details, location,
           or the account you are logged in with. The IDs are random and cannot be used to find out who you are.</p>
        <p>Only the shop administrator can see the statistics. If you press <strong>No thanks</strong>, nothing is counted and these cookies are not set.</p>

        <h2>Your choice</h2>
        <% if (consentChoice === 'granted') { %>
            <p>You have <strong>accepted</strong> anonymous visit statistics.</p>
            <form action="/privacy/consent" method="post">
                <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
                <input type="hidden" name="next" value="/privacy">
                <button type="submit" name="choice" value="decline" class="btn btn-outline">Stop counting my visits and delete the cookies</button>
            </form>
        <% } else if (consentChoice === 'declined') { %>
            <p>You have <strong>declined</strong> anonymous visit statistics.</p>
            <form action="/privacy/consent" method="post">
                <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
                <input type="hidden" name="next" value="/privacy">
                <button type="submit" name="choice" value="accept" class="btn">Accept anonymous visit statistics</button>
            </form>
        <% } else { %>
            <p>You have not chosen yet. Use the notice at the bottom of the page.</p>
        <% } %>
        <p class="muted">Declining deletes the two cookies from your browser. Visits already counted stay in the statistics, but without
           the cookie they can no longer be linked to you.</p>
    </div>
</section>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
